// EXPECT: E0271 — a call to a procedure with a `$N` comptime-value parameter (ADR-0087 §3)
//
// `$N: s64` marks a parameter polymorphic over a compile-time-known value — the value-side mirror of a
// `$T` type parameter. Its surface works: the declaration parses, formats, and its body type-checks (`N`
// is a genuine `s64`, so `return N + 1;` below is fine, where a `$T` template's body cannot be checked at
// all). What is deferred to this sub-wave's second half is **instantiation**: evaluating the argument to a
// compile-time constant at the call site and appending a concrete procedure per value.
//
// So the call is refused, by design, exactly as a `$T` call was refused (E0268) before ADR-0082 made it
// run. This is a refusal that names what arrives later, not a silent gap — the construct parses and
// checks, so nothing is lowered to a placeholder.
//
// **One** refusal, and the file lowers cleanly: the template's body checks, the call yields a poisoned
// type, and the poison propagates rather than lowering to nothing — this directory's one-diagnostic-per-file
// contract. **No `#import "Basic"`**, and the only call is to the local `$N` procedure, so nothing else can
// raise a second diagnostic: the sema corpus harness resolves without modules, where a call to an imported
// `exit` would be an unresolved name (the reason `$T`'s own call refusal lives here with no import too).

// A comptime-value parameter. Its body type-checks here — `N` is an ordinary `s64`.
make :: ($N: s64) -> s64 {
    return N + 1;
}

caller :: () -> s64 {
    // The refusal: a call needs `N`'s value evaluated at compile time, the second half of the sub-wave.
    return make(5);
}
